codex
The first prototype is correct but fails H: a naïve “fix the first conflicting completion edge” rule solved every tested instance, and direct recovery of the forced \(H\)-coloring also solved nearly all of them. That is exactly the construction leak G6 is meant to catch, so I’m not treating it as a candidate.

I’m tightening the generator so recolorings interact through overlapping Kempe chains; if the paper’s full inner-loop invariant remains unnecessary, this family will be rejected rather than dressed up as hard.
