The chordal-completion draft fails both the adversary gate and Track B’s cost-gap test, so I’m switching to the paper’s genuinely unresolved tight regime: 3-color Kempe reconfiguration on 2-degenerate rectangular grids. The paper itself singles out grids as 2-degenerate with unbounded treewidth, while its polynomial theorems do not cover the shipping grids. Certificates will be planted random Kempe walks and graded by exact replay.
