The replacement file is incomplete, but its underlying construction is stronger than the chordal prototype: it stays in the paper’s tight, unresolved regime—3-colorings of 2-degenerate grids with unbounded treewidth—and inverse-generates exact paths by composing random Kempe changes. The generator already rejects instances solved by forward/reverse greedy, discrepancy outliers, random restarts, or the natural bidirectional component-state search.

I’m preserving that construction and completing its missing public interface and gates. I will keep the Track A claim narrowly stated as “no known efficient method for this filtered grid distribution,” not infer average-case hardness from worst-case PSPACE-hardness.
