28:The shipping 10×10 grid uses (d=2,k=3), has treewidth 10, maximum degree 4, and average degree 3.6. Thus it is outside the paper’s three polynomial regimes: Theorem 0.1 needs maximum degree at most (k); Theorem 0.2 needs maximum average degree strictly below (k); and Theorem 0.3 needs treewidth at most (k-1). This is not an average-case theorem for the planted distribution. The evidence for that narrower distributional claim is G5/G6: the width-256 bidirectional component beam generated 1,371,118 successors over eight instances (171,389 mean), took 6.29 seconds total in the final run, and solved 0/8.
