Implemented the verified Track A generator based on the paper’s tight \(d=2,k=3\) Kempe-reconfiguration regime. The [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2112.02313v1) explicitly identifies grids as 2-degenerate with unbounded treewidth.

Local results:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five adversarial attacks: 0/8 each.
- Strongest beam attack: mean 171,389 successors per instance.
- 40 additional shipping instances built and verified with 40 distinct keys.
- Shipping answer: 111 characters, 32 atoms, 225 intended operations.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/gen_2112_02313.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/README.md)
