codex
A further scalability audit found that the original `escalate()` jumped grid sides by two and raised the endpoint-distance threshold too aggressively, making some later construction calls fail before the answer cap. I’m correcting the ladder to grow the ambient grid one side at a time while holding the 16-move witness and Hamming threshold fixed; this follows the “grow the haystack, not the needle” requirement and keeps all harness-reachable escalations constructible.
apply patch
