Implemented a native Track A Kempe-reconfiguration generator based on [arXiv:2112.02313](https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.02313).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/gen_2112_02313.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2112.02313/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass. Highlights:

- 0/200,000 random guesses succeeded.
- Six attacks succeeded 0/8 each.
- Exact bidirectional BFS exhausted 220,000 successors per instance.
- 140/140 relabelling checks passed; 20/20 unrelated keys were distinct.
- Shipping answer: 111 characters, 32 atoms, 225 intended operations.
- Four additional escalation rungs constructed and verified.

The external hardening requirement remains blocked: every bare, hinted, and placebo oracle redraw returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded.” These are correctly recorded as errors, not model failures, so the directory should not be submitted as hardened until the quota is restored and the harness is rerun.
